# What the constructor of a built-in base class defines on the instance comes before the prototype of the compiled class. The table lists the names that an error is made with: one of them read on an instance may be anything, and any other name is found where the class has it. It lists length for an array, which is read through its entry and never through a getter of the class, and nothing for a map, whose methods are found alone
